From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: James Morris <jmorris@namei.org>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/9] lib: sbi: stop a hart whose domain switch fails to
 program its PMP

switch_to_next_domain_context() ignores the result of
sbi_hart_protection_reconfigure(). When the target domain needs more
PMP entries than the hart has, the old entries are already disabled and
only some of the new ones are programmed, yet the hart goes on to run
the target domain. Stop the hart in M-mode instead.

When the target domain has not run on this hart before, the switch
enters it directly and never returns to the trap frame it has just
saved. The scratch area still points at that frame as the current trap
context, so the next trap, taken at the same stack address, records
itself as its own previous context and sbi_trap_error() never finishes
walking the chain. Clear the pointer before entering the new context.

AI-assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), in the GitHub Copilot CLI
---
 lib/sbi/sbi_domain_context.c | 16 +++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/lib/sbi/sbi_domain_context.c b/lib/sbi/sbi_domain_context.c
index bb505fb..cf8d157 100644
--- a/lib/sbi/sbi_domain_context.c
+++ b/lib/sbi/sbi_domain_context.c
@@ -117,6 +117,7 @@ static int switch_to_next_domain_context(struct hart_context *ctx,
 	struct sbi_trap_context *trap_ctx;
 	struct sbi_domain *current_dom, *target_dom;
 	struct sbi_scratch *scratch = sbi_scratch_thishart_ptr();
+	int rc;
 
 	if (!ctx || !dom_ctx || ctx == dom_ctx)
 		return SBI_EINVAL;
@@ -176,13 +177,26 @@ static int switch_to_next_domain_context(struct hart_context *ctx,
 	 * is also required for some of the above CSR updates (such
 	 * as satp CSR).
 	 */
-	sbi_hart_protection_reconfigure(scratch, current_dom, target_dom);
+	rc = sbi_hart_protection_reconfigure(scratch, current_dom, target_dom);
+	if (rc) {
+		/* The hart must not run with a partly programmed protection */
+		sbi_printf("%s: hart%u protection for domain %s failed (error %d)\n",
+			   __func__, current_hartid(), target_dom->name, rc);
+		sbi_hart_hang();
+	}
 
 	/* Mark current context structure initialized because context saved */
 	ctx->initialized = true;
 
 	/* If target domain context is not initialized or runnable */
 	if (!dom_ctx->initialized) {
+		/*
+		 * The trap frame saved above is never returned to, so it must
+		 * not stay the current trap context: the next trap from the
+		 * new context reuses its address and would link to itself.
+		 */
+		sbi_trap_set_context(scratch, NULL);
+
 		/* Startup boot HART of target domain */
 		if (current_hartid() == target_dom->boot_hartid)
 			sbi_hart_switch_mode(target_dom->boot_hartid,
